/** \file klip_config.dox
 * \brief Configuration dictionary for klipReduce.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup klipreduce_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * \page klip_configuration_dictionary klipReduce configuration dictionary
 *
 * This dictionary adds KLIP settings to the shared \ref common_configuration_dictionary
 * "common configuration dictionary". Long options use `--dotted.key value`; configuration files require a bare key
 * under `[section]`, as described in the shared dictionary. The key/value columns use dotted shorthand only to keep
 * the tables compact. For example, `klip.Nmodes=1,5,10` means:
 *
 * \code{.ini}
 * [klip]
 * Nmodes=1,5,10
 * \endcode
 *
 * \section klip_app_dictionary Application modes and postprocessing
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--mode` | `mode=basic` | `basic`, `normal`, `postprocess` | `basic` | `basic` and `normal` run a configured KLIP reduction. `postprocess` reads saved residual products and reapplies final-stage processing. |
 * | `--showTiming` | `showTiming=true` | bool | `false` | Print the completed KLIP reduction timing report to standard output. It is ignored by `postprocess`. |
 * | `--postprocess.directory` | `postprocess.directory=/path` | readable directory | unset | Location of saved PSF-subtracted FITS products for `postprocess`. |
 * | `--postprocess.prefix` | `postprocess.prefix=psfsub_` | literal string | unset | Saved-product filename prefix. |
 * | `--postprocess.extension` | `postprocess.extension=.fits` | literal extension | `.fits` | Saved-product filename extension. |
 *
 * \section klip_geometry_dictionary Search geometry
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--geom.minRadius` | `geom.minRadius=6,8,10` | comma-separated real pixels | required for reduction | Inner radii of KLIP search regions. Pair each entry with `maxRadius`; omit for `preProcess.only=true`. |
 * | `--geom.maxRadius` | `geom.maxRadius=8,10,12` | matching real-pixel vector | required for reduction | Outer radii of KLIP search regions. Pair each entry with `minRadius`; omit for `preProcess.only=true`. |
 * | `--geom.minAngle` | `geom.minAngle=0,90` | optional real-degree vector | unset | Lower angular bounds for wedges. Omit both angle vectors for complete annuli. |
 * | `--geom.maxAngle` | `geom.maxAngle=90,180` | optional matching real-degree vector | unset | Upper angular bounds for wedges. |
 * | `--geom.nWedges` | `geom.nWedges=N` | positive integer | `0` | Generates equal angular wedges and overrides explicit angle vectors; radius vectors are expanded to match the resulting regions. |
 *
 * Regions determine both computational cost and locality. Use several narrow annuli/wedges when spatial variation is
 * important, but ensure each contains enough unmasked pixels for the requested KL modes.
 *
 * \section klip_library_dictionary ADI exclusion and reference inclusion
 *
 * A target frame's library first applies the minimum and maximum ADI exclusions, then the configured inclusion rule.
 * The realized number of references can vary by target, especially with RDI or angle/time exclusions.
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--adi.excludeMethod` | `adi.excludeMethod=none` | `none`, `pixel`, `angle`, `imno` | `none` | Quantity used for the minimum exclusion around a target frame. |
 * | `--adi.minDPx` | `adi.minDPx=value` | nonnegative real | `0` | Minimum difference at the inner edge of the region, interpreted by `excludeMethod`. |
 * | `--adi.excludeMethodMax` | `adi.excludeMethodMax=none` | `none`, `pixel`, `angle`, `imno` | `none` | Quantity used for an optional maximum exclusion. |
 * | `--adi.maxDPx` | `adi.maxDPx=value` | nonnegative real | `0` | Maximum difference at the inner edge, interpreted by `excludeMethodMax`. |
 * | `--klip.includeMethod` | `klip.includeMethod=all` | `all`, `corr`, `time`, `angle`, `imno` | `all` | Ordering/selection method applied after exclusions. |
 * | `--klip.includeRefNum` | `klip.includeRefNum=N` | nonnegative integer | `0` (all) | Maximum retained references after exclusion and ordering. |
 *
 * `pixel` expresses motion at the inner search radius, `angle` uses field rotation, `imno` uses image-number spacing,
 * and `time` uses configured FITS dates. A missing/disabled date key cannot support meaningful time selection.
 *
 * \section klip_solver_dictionary Target-exclusion solver choice
 *
 * The shared \ref common_solver_dictionary "solver configuration" controls the KLIP implementation used after an
 * ADI exclusion. `explicitRefit` is the default. `factorDowndateExact` is eligible only for same-cube ADI exclusion
 * with `klip.includeMethod=all`; RDI, limited-reference selection, and an unusable complete base continue through the
 * direct retained-library solve. `KLEXCLSV`, `KLEXCLFT`, `KLEXCLFB`, and `KLEXCLBK` in the science output distinguish
 * the realized solver, target count, fallbacks, and configured factor backend.
 *
 * Use `leadingCovariance` when more than one reference may be excluded. Use `rankOneSecular` only when every target
 * is expected to exclude exactly one reference, normally `adi.excludeMethod=imno` with the target frame itself held
 * out. Other target patterns retain exactness by falling back to `explicitRefit` and incrementing `KLEXCLFB`:
 *
 * \code{.ini}
 * [adi]
 * excludeMethod=imno
 *
 * [solver]
 * exclusionSolver=factorDowndateExact
 * deletionBackend=rankOneSecular
 * \endcode
 *
 * Controlled single-image KLIP measurements show that `rankOneSecular` is strongly hardware- and parallelism-dependent.
 * With one BLAS thread, a region of about 200 pixels was faster from 16 references upward; at about 1,100 pixels it
 * broke even around 64 references and became clearly favorable near 128; at roughly 5,000 pixels and above it remained
 * two to five times slower through the tested 256 references. For the NACO _AF Lep_ reference configuration, the selected
 * factor path completed in 46.9 seconds rather than 110.9 seconds (2.36x _faster_) on an older 20 thread Intel Laptop, with science-product SNR
 * differences of order 1e-5 relative. The identical configuration on a newer 48 thread AMD workstation completed in 16.5
 * seconds rather than 2.93 seconds (6.45x _slower_): direct eigensolves scaled much better there.
 *
 * These are workload measurements, not a universal threshold. Retain `explicitRefit` by default, and benchmark both
 * solvers for a representative annulus, mode count, OpenMP worker count, and BLAS-thread setting on every intended
 * production host. Do not transfer a solver choice from a desktop or modest-core machine to a many-core host without
 * that comparison.
 *
 * \section klip_pca_dictionary KL basis and residual products
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--klip.Nmodes` | `klip.Nmodes=1,5,10` | comma-separated positive integers | required for reduction | Requested retained KL-mode counts. The list order is the output-cube plane order. Counts beyond a realized library's available degrees of freedom use all available modes. Omit for `preProcess.only=true`. |
 * | `--klip.meanSubMethod` | `klip.meanSubMethod=imageMean` | `imageMean`, `imageMedian`, `meanImage`, `medianImage` | `imageMean` | Mean/median subtraction convention used while constructing the KL basis. |
 * | `--klip.pixelTSNormMethod` | `klip.pixelTSNormMethod=none` | `none`, `rms` | `none` | Per-pixel temporal normalization for the PCA library. |
 * | `--klip.pixelTSSigma` | `klip.pixelTSSigma=value` | positive real | `3` | Sigma threshold used where the selected normalization needs clipping. |
 * | `--klip.rightReason` | `klip.rightReason=true` | bool | `false` | Enables the specialized right-reason masked projection diagnostic. |
 * | `--klip.rrRadius` | `klip.rrRadius=pixels` | positive real pixels | `2.5` | Radius defining the right-reason mask. |
 *
 * For each realized reference library, KLIP automatically solves the smaller of the reference-image and pixel-space
 * Gram matrices. This has no configuration switch: it preserves the requested mode list while avoiding an expensive
 * large eigensolve for small regions with many references.
 * Direct KLIP uses the fixed M32D64 precision policy: it forms the covariance and performs surrounding calculation in
 * FP32, then promotes the covariance for an FP64 eigensolve. Precision is not a configuration backend. The opt-in
 * `factorDowndateExact` solver remains FP64 internally before returning modes to FP32 storage.
 *
 * \section klip_diagnostics_dictionary Diagnostics
 *
 * | CLI | Config key/value shorthand | Type and limits | Default | Meaning |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | `--klip.writeDiagnostics` | `klip.writeDiagnostics=true` | bool | `false` | Write intermediate region, covariance, and library-selection FITS diagnostics. |
 * | `--klip.diagnosticDirectory` | `klip.diagnosticDirectory=/path` | writable directory | `.` | Destination for enabled KLIP diagnostics. Missing parent directories are created automatically. |
 *
 * Diagnostics are for audit and tuning; they do not change the calculated residuals. In particular, the covariance
 * diagnostic retains the historical reference-frame covariance representation.
 *
 * @}
 */
